// The Files plugin lets network shares be declared from its web page, and
// then asks systemd to mount them. The service runs as the unprivileged
// `ritornello` user with NoNewPrivileges=true, so `sudo` and any setuid path
// are structurally unavailable: starting a unit through polkit is the
// mechanism, and this file is the authorisation.
//
// Scoped to ONE unit on purpose, via action.lookup("unit"). Granting
// `manage-units` without that check would hand the web UI the right to start,
// stop and restart every unit on the machine -- sshd and the firewall
// included. The check is what keeps the grant proportionate to the need.
//
// The unit it does grant runs a root binary that mounts what
// /etc/ritornello/media-roots.toml declares -- and that file is written by an
// unprivileged process, from the web page. Whoever reaches the web UI
// therefore decides what root mounts, which is why the binary revalidates
// everything it reads rather than trusting the validation done on the writing
// side: forced mount point (/mnt/ritornello/<name>, never read from the
// configuration), a closed option list with no pass-through to `mount -o`, and
// no comma, space or ".." allowed in a host or share name -- mount.cifs
// options being comma-separated, a host "nas,uid=0" would otherwise inject an
// option into the line root executes.
//
// Deliberately NOT merged into 50-ritornello-power.rules: that file grants the
// power actions and says so. Keeping this grant separate means each file can
// state exactly what it opens and why, and this one can be left out on an
// appliance that has no network share.
//
// There is no capability probe on the caller's side: logind answers
// CanPowerOff, systemd has no equivalent for manage-units. The plugin tries,
// and reports systemctl's own words -- which name this file when it is
// missing.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
  if (
    subject.user === "ritornello" &&
    action.id === "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units" &&
    action.lookup("unit") === "ritornello-media-mount.service"
  ) {
    return polkit.Result.YES;
  }
});
